19. Subjects with oral administration impossible, or in the conditions of malabsorption as determined by the investigator, such as dysphagia and intestinal obstruction, etc.;
20. Subjects with significant liver cirrhosis, hepatatrophy, portal hypertension, or more than moderate volume of ascites;
21. A history of organ transplant;
22. A history of other severe systemic disease, or not suitable as determined by the investigator due to any other reasons;
23. A history of inoculation with live vaccine within 28 days prior to first dose. Note: Seasonal influenza vaccine is a broadly inactivated vaccine and is permitted. Inactivated COVID-19 vaccines are permitted. COVID-19 mRNA vaccines are not allowed. Intranasal influenza vaccines are live vaccines and are not allowed.

